 ] Call out that test_every_ci_pytest_lane_has_a_per_test_hang_guard (test_ci_workflow_parity.py:721) currently REQUIRES `--timeout=` on every lane and must be edited so a flag-less shared-tier lane is accepted when the ini keys are asserted present/positive/thread — this is a modification of existing assertions, not a new test.","cohort":["E4"],"criteria":["E4"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.1,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py:721 test_every_ci_pytest_lane_has_a_per_test_hang_guard","tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py:746 `assert \"--timeout=\" in body`","tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py:659-684 _all_workflow_pytest_steps walks all .github/workflows including _build-and-test.yml"],"finding":"Step 3 removes --timeout/--timeout-method from both _build-and-test.yml shared-tier lanes, but the existing test_every_ci_pytest_lane_has_a_per_test_hang_guard (test_ci_workflow_parity.py:721) hard-asserts `assert \"--timeout=\" in body` and `assert \"--timeout-method=thread\" in body` for EVERY pytest lane returned by _all_workflow_pytest_steps — which sweeps _build-and-test.yml. Dropping the flags trips this existing sweep, yet the plan describes the sweep only as accepting 'the asserted ini keys' for flag-less lanes, i.e. it presumes a rewrite the plan does not spell out as a modification of already-existing assertions.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f471abc5de6dfba34","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan step 3 / step 6 hang-guard sweep / AC 'Every CI pytest lane has a per-test hang guard'","norm_id":"n9914f888fe280435","priority":0.9,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The flags are removed per step 3 but the sweep's blanket `assert \"--timeout=\" in body` is left as-is; the two shared-tier lanes now fail the sweep."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"broken_oracle","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"high","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["1 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"Justify why the floor hook must be a PERMANENT mechanism rather than a transitional device, or replace it with a simpler bootstrap that self-retires once main no longer carries a sub-ini `--timeout` (e.g. land the flag removal in a first step / rely on rebase), given steps 1+3 already make the ini authoritative for every ongoing lane.","cohort":["A1"],"criteria":["A1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Part 3: 'the Verified gate executes the workflow files from TRUSTED MAIN … main's stale flag overrode the patchset's ini'","Step 3: 'REMOVE --timeout=20 --timeout-method=thread from both shared-tier lanes (single source; drift becomes impossible)' — after this, no shared-tier lane passes a CLI --timeout at all","Step 2: 'FLOOR, not blanket: a blanket marker would silently LOWER the live lanes' larger calibrated CLI budgets (900/600/1800/3600 s) since marker > CLI' — i.e. the floor is designed NOT to act on any live lane","Final AC ties the floor's proof to a single run under main's stale --timeout=20","search_files: `_timeout_floor` and `PYTEST_TIMEOUT` have no existing consumers in the repo"],"finding":"Step 2's `tests/_timeout_floor.py` + the permanent `pytest_collection_modifyitems` floor hook is machinery for a one-time bootstrap window: by the plan's own Part 3 and final AC, its sole purpose is to keep the ini budget authoritative during THIS change's Verified run while trusted main still executes the stale `--timeout=20` CLI flag. Step 3 removes that flag from main on merge, and every ongoing lane either passes NO CLI --timeout (shared tier, local `make test`) or a CLI budget ABOVE the ini that the floor explicitly refuses to lower (900/600/1800/3600 s live lanes, since marker>CLI). So after this change lands the floor can never fire for any legitimate scenario, yet the module + a per-session collection hook run on every test session forever.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fa37e54083acc50af","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan step 2 (NEW tests/_timeout_floor.py + conftest.pytest_collection_modifyitems); AC 'while still executing main's stale --timeout=20, so a green run is itself the discriminating proof of the floor'","norm_id":"n6888e9f7dfa2b190","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["After merge: every future test session runs the floor hook's precedence computation and finds nothing to floor (no lane passes a sub-ini CLI --timeout), so the hook is permanent dead weight","A reviewer maintaining conftest.py must reason about an item-marker-injection path that only ever mattered for one Verified run"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Split the change: land step 1 (ini timeout=300) + step 3 (drop the CLI --timeout from both shared-tier lanes) — that alone makes the ini authoritative for all ongoing lanes, since pytest-timeout precedence is CLI>INI and no lane then passes a sub-ini CLI flag. If the Verified-run-under-stale-main window genuinely must be bridged, prefer a bounded transitional measure over a permanent conftest hook (e.g. accept the one red Verified run and re-run post-rebase, or a temporary marker removed in a follow-up), so no floor machinery outlives the bootstrap.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.4286,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"na","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Reconcile the root-cause premise (main @6a5c88027c5 carries `timeout = 20` and `--timeout=20`) with the working tree, which already shows `timeout = 300` (pyproject.toml:662) and `--timeout=300` in both _build-and-test.yml lanes (666,681) and no `--timeout=20`: cite the exact SHA/diff establishing the 20 s state, or restate the plan against the tree's actual current values.","cohort":["E4"],"criteria":["E4"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.8,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["pyproject.toml:662 `timeout = 300` (not 20)",".github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml:666,681 `--timeout=300 --timeout-method=thread`","search for `timeout=20` in _build-and-test.yml: (no matches)"],"finding":"The plan's entire root cause rests on the premise that pristine origin/main @6a5c88027c5 carries `timeout = 20` in pyproject.toml and `--timeout=20 --timeout-method=thread` in both _build-and-test.yml lanes. The repo-scoped tools cannot corroborate that snapshot: the working tree already shows `timeout = 300` (pyproject.toml:662) and `--timeout=300` in both lanes (_build-and-test.yml:666,681), with no `--timeout=20` anywhere. The 20 s premise (and the 'zero Failed: Timeout / 11 crashes' reproduction it explains) is therefore unverifiable from the material the tools can read.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f8bbd45b6a4e888b7","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan sections 'Symptom' and 'Root cause — Part 1' (commit 6a5c88027c5 cut 300->20)","norm_id":"n3772385ffa0b3bef","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:plan-goal-satisfied","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A reviewer/implementer takes the plan at its word that main is at 20 s and diffs against a working tree already at 300 s, and cannot locate the state the root cause describes."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2857,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"yes","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"na","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"Confirm whether re-implementing pytest-timeout's CLI>env>INI precedence in-repo is necessary at all once the shared-tier lanes pass no CLI `--timeout` (the dependency already makes the ini authoritative), and drop the hand-rolled precedence walk if it is not.","cohort":["A1"],"criteria":["A1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":"novelty","evidence":["Part 3: 'pytest-timeout precedence is CLI > INI' — the dependency owns this resolution; with no CLI flag the ini already wins","Step 2 restates 'pytest-timeout's own order' and re-implements it in-repo to compute an effective budget","search_files: no repo code reads `PYTEST_TIMEOUT`, so the env arm of the re-implemented precedence serves no existing consumer"],"finding":"The floor re-derives pytest-timeout's own budget precedence (CLI > PYTEST_TIMEOUT env > ini) inside tests/_timeout_floor.py in order to invert a single edge of it, rebuilding logic the installed dependency already owns. pytest-timeout ALREADY makes the ini budget authoritative whenever no CLI flag is present — the exact condition step 3 guarantees for the shared tier — so the precedence walk (including the PYTEST_TIMEOUT env arm, which has no consumer anywhere in the repo) exists only to override th